DECL	{"args":[{"name":"u","sort":{"sort":"track"}},{"name":"r","sort":{"sort":"region"}}],"body":{"rises":{"not":{"args":[{"var":"u"},{"var":"r"}],"atom":"rel_occupies","params":[]}}},"contract":"The road user's footprint ceases to overlap a structure region at the observation: it does not overlap the region at the observation and did overlap it at the observation before. The concept is the event of that ceasing to overlap, read at the observation at which the overlap has ended, and not the state of lying outside the region at the later observations. It states no direction of departure, no carrier the road user leaves through, no speed and no place outside the region. Not a stand-in for: lying outside the region, which the occupancy relation carries on its own; a later observation at which the road user is still outside; the carrier or the way the road user goes on to, which a caller reads with its own relations; a crossing of a boundary the source represents by no region; or an entry into the region, which has its own concept.","definition":null,"id":"drv.motion.region_exit","kind":"formula","narrowings":[],"params":[],"residues":[],"supersedes":null}
